53
00:03:48.317 --> 00:03:51.303
Grammar focus: C1 grammar review.

54
00:03:51.603 --> 00:03:54.067
Let's review the key C1 structures.

55
00:03:54.367 --> 00:04:03.077
Inversion, cleft sentences, fronting, hedging, nominalisation, the subjunctive and mixed conditionals.

56
00:04:03.377 --> 00:04:06.735
For example: Never have I seen such progress.

57
00:04:07.035 --> 00:04:15.002
At C1, grammar is a tool for precision and style: choose structures to control emphasis, formality and tone.

58
00:04:16.017 --> 00:04:19.517
Now read and listen. Rithy's Journey to C1.

59
00:04:19.817 --> 00:04:25.694
When Rithy began Online Advanced, he could communicate well but often lacked precision.

60
00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:33.290
Over sixty units, he explored topics from artificial intelligence to the ethics of memory.

61
00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:39.729
He learned to hedge his claims, to structure arguments and to adapt his register.

62
00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:45.837
His vocabulary grew from everyday words to sophisticated academic expressions.

63
00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:50.879
Debates with Ms. Sarah sharpened his critical reasoning and confidence.

64
00:04:52.183 --> 00:04:57.527
In his final research presentation, he argued for climate justice in the Mekong region.

65
00:04:58.817 --> 00:05:03.173
Never had his teachers seen such a clear and nuanced performance.

66
00:05:04.483 --> 00:05:11.127
Now, with C1 achieved, his next goal is the highest level of all: C2 Proficiency.

67
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:15.034
